  "note": "Conditioned via tools/blender/condition_ai_batch.py from the staged Quaternius stash (<content-root>/external/quaternius/, see its MANIFEST.md), with keep_material=true: the conditioner PRESERVES each pack’s source material (baseColorTexture + UVs, or its flat multi-material slots) and stamps the engine contract around it (single COLOR_0 + primitive collider + larger-than-life scale + neutral COLOR_0 so it can’t tint the texture), so these render multi-tone, not flat silhouettes. Textureless FBX packs whose colour lives in flat material slots round-trip multi-tone too; degenerate alpha (invisible FBX imports) is repaired to opaque. Placed in public/tracks/prop-showcase.json props[] as cc0/<id> for validation only — level placement is the designer’s job. CC0 needs no attribution; source pack + model recorded for lineage. RIGGED/ANIMATED props (entries with \"animated\": true — the Animated Fish Pack) go through a DIFFERENT lane: tools/blender/ship_animated_prop.py, which is skinning-preserving (the static conditioner decimates/recenters/bakes a collider and would blob the rig). It keeps the armature skin + the 'Swim' clip intact, renames it to 'Swim', wraps the rig in a prop_root, stamps neutral COLOR_0, and exports with skins+animations ON. Runtime side: src/engine/render/animated-props.ts builds a THREE.AnimationMixer per placement. Animated props are render-only decoration (no collider).",
